sistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-938-fba70db6fbf5/docs/case-studies/issue-938/README.md) contains the complete requirement timeline, per-handler migration matrix, and the decision that #413 should have expanded in the same PR because repo-wide construction was its stated acceptance criterion. Incremental migration is appropriate only after the shared abstraction exists or when a partial result has an explicit tracked blocker.\n\nThe red-first test was authored through the real Formal AI server and Agent CLI. Session `ses_ffc90c6ceffewpKNqZTYUy2nYF`, its task, run log, and exported session are committed beside the case study; commit `8a1f8f76` carries the required evidence trailers.\n\nThis change has no visual UI component, so before/after screenshots and visual-regression coverage are not applicable.\n","closedAt":"2026-08-15T07:16:52Z","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSbOoU88AAAABO_hi8w","author":{"login":"konard"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\nImplemented and finalized [PR #1011](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/1011).\n\n- Added a shared data-backed meta-algorithm builder across five Rust and browser coding paths.\n- Added red-first regression tests, manual example, parser experiment, multilingual data, and case study.\n- Preserved atomic test, implementation, and documentation commits.\n- Full Rust suite: 3,730 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored.\n- Browser suite: 75 passed.\n- Formatting, Clippy, examples, doctests, and all repository policy gates passed.\n- All 12 fresh CI workflows passed for head `8ba73cfa`.\n- PR is ready, mergeable, and reports `CLEAN`.\n- Working tree is clean. No failed-run logs were needed.\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*","createdAt":"2026-08-15T07:13:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/1011